 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "n units are bought one after another. For each unit a market price x is drawn uniformly at random from the integers a, a+1, ..., b (discrete model, inferred), independently per unit. After seeing x the buyer pays either x or the fixed price p; the fixed price may be used at most k times in total. Return the minimum expected total cost under an optimal policy, rounded half up to exactly six decimal places, as a decimal string.",
